  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nIf cotA = (5)/(12)\n\n**Formula used:**\n\ncotA = (adjacent)/(opposite)\n\nsecA = (hypotenuse)/(adjacent)\n\ncosecA = (hypotenuse)/(opposite)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nFor cotA = (5)/(12)\n\nLet opposite = 12k and adjacent = 5k\n\n⇒ hypotenuse = √((12k)² + (5k)²)\n\n⇒ hypotenuse = √(144k² + 25k²)\n\n⇒ hypotenuse = √(169k²)\n\n⇒ hypotenuse = 13k\n\nsecA = (hypotenuse)/(adjacent) = (13k)/(5k) = 13/5\n\ncosecA = (hypotenuse)/(opposite) = (13k)/(12k) = 13/12\n\nGiven expression: √((secA - cosecA)) / √((secA + cosecA)) - √((17)/(7))\n\n⇒ √((13/5 - 13/12)) / √((13/5 + 13/12)) - √((17)/(7))\n\n⇒ √((156 - 65)/60) / √((156 + 65)/60) - √((17)/(7))\n\n⇒ √((91)/(60)) / √((221)/(60)) - √((17)/(7))\n\n⇒ √((91)/(60) × (60)/(221)) - √((17)/(7))\n\n⇒ √((91)/(221)) - √((17)/(7))\n\n⇒ (√(7×13))/(√(17×13)) - √((17)/(7))\n\n⇒ √(7)/(√(17)) - √((17)/(7))\n\n⇒ √((7)/(17)) - √((17)/(7))\n\n⇒ (√((7)/(17)) - (√((17)/(7))))\n\nRationalize to get a common base:\n\n⇒ (√((7)/(17)) × √((7)/(7))) - (√((17)/(7)) × √((17)/(17)))\n\n⇒ (√((49)/(119))) - (√((289)/(119)))\n\n⇒ (7)/(√(119)) - (17)/(√(119))\n\n⇒ (7 - 17)/(√(119))\n\n⇒ -10/(√(119))\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (2).**",
